  "body": "#1198 slice (b): move handles with drag-to-move. Slice (a), the bottom bar, merged in #1203. Slice (c), the rotate handles, is #2047. Slice (d), snapping and typed values, stays on #1198.\r\n\r\n**GUI hand check needed.** The kittest harness and headless state tests test the handles, the drag and the readout. The offscreen screenshots below come from the same harness. Nobody has examined them on a real screen with real mouse input.\r\n\r\n## What changed\r\n- **Move mode in the bottom bar.** A new bar button (a four-armed cross, after Pick through) turns `State::move_handles` on and off. It is off by default. It is view state like Pick through, and it queues no command.\r\n- **Handles** (`crates/ui/src/move_drag.rs`, painted by `crates/ui/src/egui_app/move_handles.rs`). With Move on and exactly one shown part selected, three arms in the axis colours start at the bounding-box centre of the part. Each arm ends in a ball. The arms stay 70 px long on screen at all zoom levels. The ball under the pointer is drawn larger.\r\n- **Drag.** A press on a ball takes the press before orbit and pick. A press on empty space still orbits. When a nav tool of the bar (Orbit, Pan, Zoom) is latched, that tool owns the press. While the button is down, the preview moves the body along the axis (`world.rs` draws it with an offset) and never writes the world. The signed distance shows above the bar. The distance is the point where the cursor ray is nearest to the axis line, so the part stays under the cursor in perspective and in ortho.\r\n- **One command per drag.** The release queues `CommandKind::MoveModelBy { name, delta }`. The drain (`crates/ui/src/state_move_by.rs`) runs it as the `MoveModel::new` of the Model page, with the rotation copied bit for bit. Thus a drag is one undo step, with the same staleness, the same following stock and the same fixture-clash warning as a typed move. There is no new placement path.\r\n- **No history step for:** Escape during a drag (the key is consumed), a drag that ends at its start point, and Move turned off.\r\n- **Turned setups.** When the active setup holds the part turned (#326), the drag occurs in the frame of that setup. The shown delta is rotated back into the document frame, so the part moves along the axis that the user sees.\r\n- Decisions are in `docs/decisions/1198-drag-to-move.md`: only parts are dragged in this slice, Move mode is off by default, and the preview moves the body only.\r\n\r\n## MCP\r\nNo new app command, thus no new MCP tool. `MoveModelBy` is a UI queue verb over the existing `MoveModel`. The MCP `move_model` tool (`crates/app/src/mcp/model_tools.rs`) already places a part through `MoveModel`. An agent can make each move that a drag makes.\r\n\r\n## Screenshots (offscreen, kittest harness with the headless GPU viewport)\r\nThe \"before\" is Move off on this branch: on `main` the bar has no Move button, and all else is the same.\r\n\r\n| Move off (before) | Move on |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| ![Move off](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/blob/screenshots/pr-1330/1-move-off.png?raw=true) | ![Move on](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/blob/screenshots/pr-1330/2-move-on.png?raw=true) |\r\n\r\n| X ball dragged (preview, readout above the bar) | After the release (one `MoveModel`) |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| ![Dragging](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/blob/screenshots/pr-1330/3-dragging.png?raw=true) | ![Released](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/blob/screenshots/pr-1330/4-released.png?raw=true) |\r\n\r\n## Refresh for merge (2026-11-18)\r\n- Old head: `58df4b729`. New head: `553f6c2e6` (merge of `origin/main` at `b629dc7e8`). No rebase, no force-push.\r\n- Two conflicts, resolved by hand. Both sides are kept:\r\n  - `crates/ui/src/state.rs`: the `move_by` module line of this PR and the `fixture_turn_ui` lines of main.\r\n  - `crates/ui/src/egui_app/shell.rs`: main wraps `update_hover` in `frame_cost::time`. This PR adds `|| state.body_drag.is_some()` to the press argument. The merged line has the two changes.\r\n- The resolution is the same as on #2185 (stacked on this PR).\r\n- `git diff origin/main --stat` lists only the 13 files of this PR. No snapshot PNG changed.\r\n\r\n## How tested (on head `3d394d6f4`, debug, `-j 6`, `--test-threads=6`)\r\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 17 steps, 0 failed. camcraft-ui lib: all green (the 1114 earlier tests and the 4 new ones), 7 ignored. This includes:\r\n  - `egui_app::tests::body_drag` (kittest, the real shell; 6 tests): `handles_show_only_in_move_mode_on_a_selected_part`, `a_ball_drag_is_one_undoable_move_by_the_dragged_distance`, `escape_mid_drag_cancels_with_no_history_step`, `a_drag_that_ends_where_it_began_adds_nothing`, `empty_space_still_orbits_in_move_mode`, `focus_loss_mid_drag_cancels_and_a_later_release_sends_no_move`.\r\n  - `move_drag_tests` (headless state; 8 tests): `the_drag_distance_is_the_axis_point_under_the_cursor`, `a_press_off_the_balls_is_not_a_drag`, `a_turned_setup_moves_the_part_along_the_axis_it_shows`, `the_rotation_is_kept_bit_for_bit`, `a_non_finite_distance_is_refused_by_name`, `a_still_frame_walks_no_facets_and_a_move_walks_them_again` (the centre cache counter test), `an_axis_seen_almost_end_on_holds_the_drag`, `one_motion_step_drags_at_most_one_view_width`.\r\n  - The bar laws with the new button: `viewport_bar::tests::bar_fits_its_buttons` and `law_tests::view_cube_tests::the_hud_is_laid_out_from_the_pane_alone` (it iterates each button in `NAVS`), the structural twin and the pick-through and box-select tests.\r\n- The camcraft-ui integration suites of the quick plan (boundary, boundary_picks, catalog_render, feedback, fixtures, gpu_render, machine, models, operations, shell, sinker_setup, tap_hand, theme_example, theme_files, waterjet_tool): all green. `--test shell`: 21 passed.\r\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets --no-deps -- -D warnings`: clean.\r\n\r\n## Not exercised\r\n- A real screen and real mouse input. GUI hand check needed.\r\n- Pixel snapshots (release lane). The bar is wider, so the viewport goldens differ. They are made again at the cut. This PR changes no PNG.\r\n- The other ui integration suites and the other crates. This PR changes only `camcraft-ui` and one decision file.\r\n- Fixtures and the stock cannot be dragged (recorded decision).\r\n\r\n## Open notes for the review\r\n- The Move icon (four arms with balls) and the Pan icon (four arrows) look almost the same in the bar (see the screenshots). A reviewer must decide if one of them needs a different glyph.\r\n- `shell.rs` (1043 lines) and `viewport_bar.rs` (461 lines) were already more than 400 lines on `main` (1028 and 433). This PR adds only its own lines to them.\r\n\r\nChangelog: Viewport: a Move button in the bottom bar puts axis handles on the selected part; dragging a ball moves the part along that axis, one undo step per drag (#1198 b)\r\nEffort: high (no escalation)\r\n\r\nRefs #1198\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
